        "body": "Bug-fix release.\n\n## Python: clustering no longer crashes (#135)\n\n`learn_tree` failed with `IndexError: list index out of range` for anyone who installed SCICoNE 1.0.0 with conda. It clusters cells with PhenoGraph, whose default Louvain implementation runs executables bundled inside PhenoGraph, and in PhenoGraph 1.5.7 — the version on bioconda — the Linux one crashes.\n\nSCICoNE now uses PhenoGraph's Leiden implementation by default. It runs through `leidenalg`, already a PhenoGraph dependency, and takes the seed passed to `learn_tree`, so **clustering is now reproducible** for a given seed.\n\n**This changes clustering results** compared with installations where Louvain did work. `clustering_algo=\"louvain\"` restores the previous behaviour on `learn_tree`, `initialize_cluster_tree` and `condense_segmented_clusters`.\n\n## Command line: clear errors for a malformed counts matrix (#134)\n\nA counts matrix that didn't match `--n_cells` and `--n_bins` (or `--n_regions`) — most often a transposed one — made the executables write past the end of their buffer, giving an assertion failure or a segfault depending on the machine. They now stop and report the expected and the found shape:\n\n```\nError: counts.csv: expected 9 rows by 3273 columns, but found 3273 rows by 9 columns. It looks transposed.\nThe counts matrix needs one row per cell (--n_cells=9) and one column per bin (--n_bins=3273).\n```\n\nA header row or row names are reported the same way. Trailing blank lines and Windows line endings are now accepted.\n\n## Also\n\nAn empty vector was indexed when hashing a tree node with no events. It was harmless in practice and changed no results, but it is undefined behaviour, and newer compilers reject it in debug builds.\n\n## Installing\n\n```bash\nconda install -c bioconda -c conda-forge scicone=1.0.1\n```\n\nonce the bioconda update is merged. Until then, the Python package — which carries the clustering fix — can be installed from this release over an existing 1.0.0:\n\n```bash\npip install --no-deps --force-reinstall \"git+https://github.com/cbg-ethz/SCICoNE.git@v1.0.1#subdirectory=pyscicone\"\n```\n",
        "created_at": "2026-11-24T13:20:00Z",
